{1 elm_playground_gamekits }

What the games of a genre share, written from scratch for teaching: how
each genre works, a kit per genre, one idea per module. They are above
the {{:../elm_playground/index.html} Elm Playground}, most of them drawing
with it, and use the from-scratch libraries of
{{:../tiny_libs/index.html} tiny_libs} (ai, audio).

Each is a library of its own, named [elm_playground_gamekits.<name>]
outside this repository, for example in a dune file:

{v
(executable
 (name main)
 (libraries elm_playground elm_playground_native
            elm_playground_gamekits.kit_platformer))
v}

The libraries are unwrapped: their modules are used by their own names,
[Tile_move], [Ladder].

{2:shmup Shoot 'em ups}

Shots as values that move, the curves enemies fly along
([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_shmup]):

{!modules: Shots Path}

{2:fighting Fighting games}

Hit boxes, a move's frames, fighters as stick figures
([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_brawler]); and in 3D, a fighter as a
skeleton of boxes ([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_brawler3d]):

{!modules: Hitbox Frame_data Stickman Skeleton}

{2:platform Platformers}

A box moved against a tilemap, ladders, shaped ground felt by sensors
([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_platformer]); Crush's slices
([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_crush]):

{!modules: Tile_move Ladder Slope Crush}

{2:arcade Mazes and arenas}

A grid's corridors and the ways chosen in them
([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_maze]); Tron's light cycles
([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_lightcycles]):

{!modules: Grid_move Chase Lightcycles}

{2:puzzle Puzzles}

Pushing on a grid, going back, Sokoban's rules, levels and solver
([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_puzzle]):

{!modules: Push Puzzle_undo Sokoban}

{2:cards Cards}

The 52 cards, Microsoft's numbered deals, a card drawn
([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_cards]):

{!modules: Cards}

{2:adventure Adventures}

The world as data and the player's sentences answered by rules
([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_adventure]):

{!modules: Adventure}

{2:racing Racing}

The road and a car on it, a car on a flat world or on ground with a
height ([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_racing]); and in 3D, a course as a
ribbon of quads ([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_racing3d]):

{!modules: Road Car Topdown Offroad Track3d}

{2:sports Sports}

The ball pushed ahead, a side keeping its shape
([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_sports]):

{!modules: Free_ball Formation}

{2:strategy Strategy}

The three kinds of order and the walking
([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_rts]):

{!modules: Orders}

{2:rhythm Rhythm games}

The music's clock, the grades, charts played and made
([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_rhythm]):

{!modules: Rhythm}

{2:worlds The worlds of 2.5D and 3D games}

Doom's sectors ([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_sectors]), Descent's mine
and its ship ([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_segments]), Comanche's
terrain ([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_heightmap]), a world seen from
one fixed angle ([elm_playground_gamekits.kit_isometric]):

{!modules: Sectors Segments Sixdof Heightmap Isometric}
